                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_02\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit renames the test file's package declaration from\n`com.github.piotr.rusin.yule` to `com.github.piotr_rusin.yule` (and moves the\nfile to the corresponding directory), with the commit message stating this\nfixes a test initialization error where \"No application configuration could\nbe found.\"\n\nTracing the package name across the candidates:\n- candidate_01 creates the initial project. Both the main application class\n  (`YuleApplication`) and the test class (`YuleApplicationTests`) are\n  consistently placed under the package `com.github.piotr.rusin.yule`. At\n  this point everything is consistent, so no bug exists yet.\n- candidate_02 renames/moves the main source files (`YuleApplication.java`,\n  `Post.java`) to the package `com.github.piotr_rusin.yule` (adding an\n  underscore), matching the Maven groupId `com.github.piotr-rusin.yule`. It\n  also adds a license header to the test file, but critically it does NOT\n  rename the test file's package \u2014 the test class is left behind in\n  `com.github.piotr.rusin.yule`. This creates a mismatch: the\n  `@SpringBootApplication` class now lives in a different package tree than\n  the `@SpringBootTest` test class. Since Spring Boot's component/context\n  scanning for tests relies on finding the `@SpringBootApplication` class in\n  the same or a parent package, this mismatch causes the \"No application\n  configuration could be found\" error referenced in the fix commit message.\n- candidate_03 is the fix itself (it is byte-for-byte the diff described in\n  fix_commit_diff.txt): it renames the test file from\n  `com.github.piotr.rusin.yule` to `com.github.piotr_rusin.yule`, restoring\n  package consistency and resolving the initialization error.\n\nSince the bug (package divergence between main and test code) was first\nintroduced when the main package was renamed without updating the test\npackage \u2014 i.e., in candidate_02 \u2014 that is the bug-introducing commit.\n"
